    standfirst: "Executives open a report and it hangs, or fails with a capacity error. On Microsoft Fabric, that is usually throttling: the capacity has borrowed so much future compute that Fabric starts delaying, then rejecting, work. Here is how the stages work, how to find the cause and how to size an F SKU.",
    blurb: "Smoothing, overage protection, interactive delay, interactive and background rejection, surge protection, the Capacity Metrics app, and the P SKU retirement timeline.",
    answer: "Fabric throttles a capacity when it has used more than ten minutes of future compute: first it delays interactive operations, then after an hour of future use it rejects them, and after 24 hours it rejects background jobs such as refreshes too. Find the workloads using the most capacity units in the Capacity Metrics app, reschedule or optimise them, use surge protection to cap background work, and size the F SKU from measured usage rather than from the old P SKU name.",
